+# Contract: Host hook registration & per-event budget matrix
+
+**Phase 1 output** of `__SPECKIT_COMMAND_PLAN__`.
+
+Purpose: a normative statement of what each host registration declares for each event, and how those declarations relate to the installed hosts' wall-clock clamps. This is the registration contract the feature touches. The format follows the host Agent-Plugin hooks schema — `hooks.<Event>[]`, each entry an optional `matcher` plus a `hooks[]` array of `{ type, command, timeout?, statusMessage?, additionalContextLimit? }`. The **only** field this feature changes is `timeout` on **Codex SessionEnd**.
+
+## Registration JSON shapes (after the change)
+
+Codex — `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/codex-hooks.json` and the byte-identical `plugins/graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/codex-hooks.json`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "hooks": {
+    "SessionStart": [
+      {
+        "matcher": "startup|resume|clear|compact",
+        "hooks": [
+          {
+            "type": "command",
+            "command": "python \"${PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/session_hook.py\" start --host codex",
+            "statusMessage": "Loading Keel and GraphHelm context",
+            "timeout": 5,
+            "additionalContextLimit": 512
+          }
+        ]
+      }
+    ],
+    "SessionEnd": [
+      {
+        "hooks": [
+          {
+            "type": "command",
+            "command": "python \"${PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/session_hook.py\" end --host codex",
+            "timeout": 3
+          }
+        ]
+      }
+    ]
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Claude — `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/hooks.json` (**unchanged**):
+
+```json
+{
+  "hooks": {
+    "SessionStart": [
+      {
+        "matcher": "startup|resume|clear|compact",
+        "hooks": [
+          { "type": "command", "command": "python \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/session_hook.py\" start --host claude", "timeout": 5 }
+        ]
+      }
+    ],
+    "SessionEnd": [
+      { "hooks": [ { "type": "command", "command": "python \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/session_hook.py\" end --host claude", "timeout": 5 } ] }
+    ]
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## Normative rules
+
+- **N1**: Codex SessionEnd `timeout == 3` in BOTH codex files; equals the installed Codex SessionEnd clamp; never exceeds the clamp (no over-declaration). *(FR-001)*
+- **N2**: Codex SessionStart `timeout == 5` (unchanged). *(FR-004)*
+- **N3**: Claude SessionStart `timeout == 5` and Claude SessionEnd `timeout == 5` (unchanged). *(FR-005)*
+- **N4**: The end-acknowledgement wait in `session_hook.py` (`W = 2.0 s` socket inactivity) satisfies `W < declared(codex, SessionEnd)` and `W <= declared(claude, SessionEnd)`. *(FR-002/FR-003)*
+- **N5**: No other registration field or file changes. *(FR-010)*
+- **N6**: The two Codex registration files remain byte-identical and the two hook scripts remain byte-identical. *(FR-007)*
+
+## Before/after delta
+
+| field | before | after |
+|-------|:------:|:-----:|
+| `codex-hooks.json` (both copies) → `SessionEnd.hooks[0].timeout` | 5 | **3** |
+| `session_hook.py` (both copies) → end POST wait | 3.0 s | **2.0 s** |
+| everything else (both `codex-hooks.json`, both `session_hook.py`, `hooks.json`, manifests) | — | byte-stable |
+
+## Observers
+
+- **Static read** of the four registration files asserting the exact matrix in N1–N3 (see `quickstart.md` S2). This checks the declarations; it is not proof on its own (gate G7), which is why S2 is paired with the behavioral run.
+- **Behavioral**: the hook test module (`quickstart.md` S3), which is the adequate observer for the delivery behavior the budgets constrain.
