+# Contract: Runtime session-end signal (HTTP)
+
+**Phase 1 output** of `__SPECKIT_COMMAND_PLAN__`.
+
+Transport: a single HTTP(S) `POST` to the local Runtime, bearer-authenticated from a token file; plain HTTP is allowed only for loopback hosts (validated in `binding()`); no redirects are followed. Request and response bodies are JSON. **This contract already exists and the feature does not change it** — it is documented here so the change's blast radius (a single client-side timeout) is provably *outside* the wire shape.
+
+## Request
+
+```
+POST /v1/executions/{executionId}/signal
+Authorization: Bearer <token>
+Content-Type: application/json
+X-GraphHelm-Actor: {host}-session-{session}
+X-GraphHelm-Actor-Type: agent
+X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session: {session}
+Idempotency-Key: session-end-v2-<24hex>
+
+{ "signal": {
+  "id": "session-end-v2-<24hex>",
+  "source": { "type": "tool", "id": "{host}-session-{session}" },
+  "type": "agent_session_ended",
+  "severity": "low",
+  "description": "{actor} session ended; task outcome was not verified by this hook.",
+  "evidence": ["<executionId>"],
+  "emittedAt": "<ISO-8601 UTC, tz-aware>"
+} }
+```
+
+## Response (success)
+
+```
+HTTP/1.1 200 OK
+{ "ok": true, "data": { "executionId": "<executionId>", "signalId": "session-end-v2-<24hex>", "decision": "<runtime decision>" } }
+```
+
+`data.executionId` and `data.signalId` **MUST echo the sent values** for the hook to mark the end delivered. Any other combination is treated as *unobserved* and stays retryable (a mismatched ack is tested: unobserved, not delivered).
+
+## Failure / non-success
+
+- A non-`ok` response, an HTTP `5xx`, or a connection reset/abort/timeout within the socket-inactivity wait ⇒ the hook prints `graphhelm-hook: end unobserved (<ErrorType>)` to stderr and does **not** record delivery (retryable). Return code remains 0; the host session is not blocked.
+- The `decision` value in an `ok:true` body (e.g., `rejected`) is a Runtime graph-mutation verdict and is **separate** from whether the signal was recorded; a rejected mutation does not mean the signal was not stored.
+
+## Semantics preserved by this feature (FR-009)
+
+- The same `signal` body and the same `Idempotency-Key` are used on every retry.
+- After a confirmed ack, later ends read the local delivery record and skip sending (request-count guarantee — a repeat end produces zero extra POSTs).
+- An unbound session makes no request at all (silent; no output, no error).
+
+## What the feature changes about this contract
+
+Nothing about the wire shape, headers, or response contract. The only related change is the **client-side socket-inactivity wait** on this request, reduced from `3.0 s` to `2.0 s`, so that the request/acknowledge round-trip completes inside the installed host's wall-clock clamp and is never killed mid-wait. This is a timing bound on the same unchanged request, not a new endpoint or field.
