+# Data Model: Codex SessionEnd Budget Clamp
+
+**Phase 1 output** of `__SPECKIT_COMMAND_PLAN__`.
+
+Scope note: no database and no persisted schema are introduced by this feature. This model documents (a) the *runtime value model* the change adjusts — the per-host/per-event budget picture and the shared acknowledgement wait — and (b) the two spec entities that carry the end-of-session observation and its local delivery state. Field-level detail mirrors what `session_hook.py` already validates, so this is authoritative-for-the-change, not a new persistence contract.
+
+## 1. Budget model (what this feature changes)
+
+Two distinct kinds of budget exist and must not be conflated (spec Key Entities).
+
+### 1a. Declared hook budget
+The `timeout` field (seconds, integer) on a hook command registration in a host's hooks JSON. The host reads it; if it exceeds the host's own clamp for that event, the host applies the clamp instead — so a larger declaration silently over-promises.
+
+Fields:
+- `host`: `codex` | `claude` (which registration family)
+- `event`: `SessionStart` | `SessionEnd`
+- `file`: the registration file that carries it
+- `declaredSeconds`: int
+- `hostEnforcedSeconds`: int — the installed host's clamp for this event (an external fact, not stored in these files)
+- Invariant (for the fix to be meaningful): `declaredSeconds <= hostEnforcedSeconds` (no over-declaration).
+
+Budget table (**before → after**):
+
+| host | file | event | declared before | declared after | hostEnforced | status |
+|------|------|-------|:---------------:|:--------------:|:------------:|--------|
+| codex | `graphhelm/hooks/codex-hooks.json` | SessionStart | 5 | 5 (unchanged) | 5* | unchanged (FR-004) |
+| codex | `graphhelm/hooks/codex-hooks.json` | SessionEnd | 5 | **3** | **3** | fixed (FR-001) |
+| codex | `graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/codex-hooks.json` | SessionStart | 5 | 5 (unchanged) | 5* | unchanged |
+| codex | `graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/codex-hooks.json` | SessionEnd | 5 | **3** | **3** | fixed (FR-001, byte-identical pair) |
+| claude | `graphhelm/hooks/hooks.json` | SessionStart | 5 | 5 (unchanged) | 5 | unchanged (FR-005) |
+| claude | `graphhelm/hooks/hooks.json` | SessionEnd | 5 | 5 (unchanged) | 5 | unchanged (FR-005) |
+
+\* The observed clamp is documented as applying to Codex **SessionEnd**; Codex SessionStart keeps its 5 declaration (assumption carried from the spec and FR-004).
+
+Validation rules:
+- Both Codex packages declare identical SessionEnd seconds (guaranteed by byte-identical files, FR-007).
+- Codex SessionEnd declared (3) equals its host clamp (3); neither Codex package over-declares.
+- Claude values are not modified in any case (FR-005).
+
+### 1b. Acknowledgement wait (socket inactivity)
+A single shared value in the hook script (`session_hook.py`), applied only to the end POST; the start GET uses a separate 1.0 s default (unchanged).
+
+Fields:
+- `name`: end-acknowledgement socket-inactivity wait
+- `before`: 3.0 s
+- `after`: **2.0 s**
+- `appliesTo`: end POST (`POST /v1/executions/{id}/signal`) in both script copies
+- `bounds`: `1.0 < W < 3.0`, and `W > 1.25` to keep the existing behavioral test green unmodified
+- Relationship: `W < hostEnforced(codex, SessionEnd)` and `W <= hostEnforced(claude, SessionEnd)` ⇒ the process can always finish its wait inside either host's wall clock (the defect being removed).
+
+## 2. Session-end signal (carries the observation)
+
+The attributed, idempotent end-of-session observation the hook POSTs to the Runtime. Shaped and revalidated by `_signal` / `_validate_delivery` in `session_hook.py`; **unchanged** by this feature.
+
+Fields:
+- `id`: `session-end-v2-<24-hex>` — SHA-256 over `v2\0{execution}\0{session}\0{host}\0{origin}` truncated to 24 hex; stable across retries.
+- `source.type`: `"tool"`
+- `source.id` (actor): `{host}-session-{session}` — session-scoped identity, not just a host name.
+- `type`: `"agent_session_ended"`
+- `severity`: `"low"`
+- `description`: `"{actor} session ended; task outcome was not verified by this hook."` (+ optional ` Declared node binding label: {node}.` when `GRAPHHELM_NODE_ID` is set)
+- `evidence`: `[execution]`
+- `emittedAt`: ISO-8601 UTC with timezone, ≤ 40 chars
+- HTTP headers: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, `X-GraphHelm-Actor: {actor}`, `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Type: "agent"`, `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session: {session}`, `Idempotency-Key: {id}`
+
+Invariants:
+- Never carries secret material (token path/value or token content must not appear in the serialized signal) — constitutional invariant, preserved because the body is untouched.
+- Identical body and identical idempotency identity across retries (FR-009).
+
+Relationship: emitted by the hook on SessionEnd when bound and not yet delivered.
+
+## 3. Local delivery record (makes repeated ends skip confirmed sends)
+
+A per-`(execution, session, host, origin)` state file on local disk.
+
+File layout: `<stateRoot>/<sha256("v2\0{execution}\0{session}\0{host}\0{origin}")>.json`, plus a sibling `.lock`.
+
+Fields (JSON, version 2):
+- `version`: 2
+- `executionId`, `sessionId`, `host`, `origin`: identity bindings (must all match on read, else `hook state identity mismatch`)
+- `briefing?`: cached, revalidated briefing digest (SessionStart; orthogonal to this change)
+- `delivery?`: object
+  - `executionId`, `sessionId`: identity
+  - `signalId`: the signal id
+  - `signal`: stored copy of the emitted signal (revalidated against identity on read)
+  - `declaredNodeId?`: optional node label
+  - `delivered`: bool — the receipt of a **confirmed** durable acknowledgement
+
+State transitions (`delivery`):
+
+```
+                       (first end, no record)
+                              |
+                              v
+                   { delivered: false }  <---------+
+                       |                            |
+        ack echoes     |   ack refused / timeout /  |
+        matching       |   mismatch / killed mid-wait
+        executionId &  v                             |
+        signalId   { delivered: true }               |
+                       |                             |
+          later ends read state -> skip send    retry with the SAME body + idempotency key
+```
+
+- `delivered:false → delivered:true` **only** when the Runtime ack echoes the matching `executionId` and `signalId` (FR-009).
+- Refusal, timeout, mismatch, or host-kill leaves `delivered:false` ⇒ **retryable** with the identical body and idempotency key (no duplicate/divergent signal). This is exactly the path the shortened wait now keeps inside the host clamp.
+- A corrupt receipt fails closed (unobserved) and never becomes delivery proof.
+
+## 4. Invariants asserted by the tests
+
+- **Byte-identity**: `hash(graphhelm session_hook.py) == hash(companion session_hook.py)` and the same for the two `codex-hooks.json`.
+- **Wiring**: companion `.codex-plugin/plugin.json["hooks"] == "./hooks/codex-hooks.json"`; version equality across the two main legacy manifests and the companion manifest; no `extensions` key in the main manifest.
+- **Request-count guarantees**: confirmed repeat end ⇒ exactly 1 POST; refusal/timeout ⇒ retryable; overlapping ends keep one signal body; a killed hook releases its lock and retries the same signal.
+
+## 5. Out of scope (data-wise)
+
+No new table, column, migration, message-queue topic, or wire field. The model above describes existing structures whose *values* change; the wire shape and local record shape are both preserved.
